{"schemaVersion":1,"generatedAt":"2026-08-16T16:20:46.501Z","id":"6f46b5dae03d6b699d1433df","canonicalUrl":"https://lore.kernel.org/r/20260812-ipq5424_i2c_scl_updates-v2-0-e09cd39d01d7%40oss.qualcomm.com/","channels":["linux-i2c"],"thread":{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"thread:lore-git:20260812-ipq5424_i2c_scl_updates-v2-0-e09cd39d01d7@oss.qualcomm.com","source":{"kind":"static-generated","canonicalThreadUrl":"https://lore.kernel.org/r/20260812-ipq5424_i2c_scl_updates-v2-0-e09cd39d01d7%40oss.qualcomm.com/","fetchedAt":"2026-08-16T16:20:46.501Z","contentDigest":"lore-git:20260812-ipq5424_i2c_scl_updates-v2-0-e09cd39d01d7@oss.qualcomm.com"},"subject":"[PATCH v2 0/2] I2C SCL counter updates for Qualcomm IPQ5424 SoC","messages":{"20260812-ipq5424_i2c_scl_updates-v2-0-e09cd39d01d7@oss.qualcomm.com":{"id":"20260812-ipq5424_i2c_scl_updates-v2-0-e09cd39d01d7@oss.qualcomm.com","messageId":"20260812-ipq5424_i2c_scl_updates-v2-0-e09cd39d01d7@oss.qualcomm.com","references":[],"missingAncestorIds":[],"author":{"name":"Kathiravan Thirumoorthy","address":"kathiravan.thirumoorthy@oss.qualcomm.com"},"replyTo":[],"to":[{"name":"Mukesh Kumar Savaliya","address":"mukesh.savaliya@oss.qualcomm.com"},{"name":"Viken Dadhaniya","address":"viken.dadhaniya@oss.qualcomm.com"},{"name":"Andi Shyti","address":"andi.shyti@kernel.org"},{"name":"Manikanta Mylavarapu","address":"quic_mmanikan@quicinc.com"},{"name":"Bjorn Andersson","address":"andersson@kernel.org"},{"name":"Konrad Dybcio","address":"konradybcio@kernel.org"}],"cc":[{"name":"Mukesh Kumar Savaliya","address":"quic_msavaliy@quicinc.com"},{"name":"","address":"linux-i2c@vger.kernel.org"},{"name":"","address":"linux-arm-msm@vger.kernel.org"},{"name":"","address":"linux-kernel@vger.kernel.org"},{"name":"Kathiravan Thirumoorthy","address":"kathiravan.thirumoorthy@oss.qualcomm.com"},{"name":"","address":"stable@vger.kernel.org"}],"timestamp":{"raw":"2026-08-12T08:30:54.000Z","iso":"2026-08-12T08:30:54.000Z","valid":true},"subject":"[PATCH v2 0/2] I2C SCL counter updates for Qualcomm IPQ5424 SoC","mailingLists":[{"id":"linux-i2c.vger.kernel.org","displayName":"linux-i2c.vger.kernel.org"}],"blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","text":"To meet the specification requirement in the standard-mode bus frequency,\nupdate the SCL counters as recommended by the design team."},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"IPQ5424 uses 32MHz source clock for the I2C and I2C is supported on both\nRTL-hardened and firmware based SEs. The driver already provides SCL timing\nparameters for a 32 MHz source clock, but the resulting I2C bus frequencies\ndo not meet the required specification on firmware-based SEs."},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"As recommended by the hardware design team, use a separate set of SCL\ntiming parameters for firmware-based SEs. Introduce a dedicated\nfrequency table and select the appropriate table based on the SE type."},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Signed-off-by: Kathiravan Thirumoorthy <kathiravan.thirumoorthy@oss.qualcomm.com>"}],"patchIds":[],"attachmentMetadata":[],"sourceOrdinal":0,"diagnostics":[]},"20260812-ipq5424_i2c_scl_updates-v2-1-e09cd39d01d7@oss.qualcomm.com":{"id":"20260812-ipq5424_i2c_scl_updates-v2-1-e09cd39d01d7@oss.qualcomm.com","messageId":"20260812-ipq5424_i2c_scl_updates-v2-1-e09cd39d01d7@oss.qualcomm.com","references":["20260812-ipq5424_i2c_scl_updates-v2-0-e09cd39d01d7@oss.qualcomm.com"],"missingAncestorIds":[],"author":{"name":"Kathiravan Thirumoorthy","address":"kathiravan.thirumoorthy@oss.qualcomm.com"},"replyTo":[],"to":[{"name":"Mukesh Kumar Savaliya","address":"mukesh.savaliya@oss.qualcomm.com"},{"name":"Viken Dadhaniya","address":"viken.dadhaniya@oss.qualcomm.com"},{"name":"Andi Shyti","address":"andi.shyti@kernel.org"},{"name":"Manikanta Mylavarapu","address":"quic_mmanikan@quicinc.com"},{"name":"Bjorn Andersson","address":"andersson@kernel.org"},{"name":"Konrad Dybcio","address":"konradybcio@kernel.org"}],"cc":[{"name":"Mukesh Kumar Savaliya","address":"quic_msavaliy@quicinc.com"},{"name":"","address":"linux-i2c@vger.kernel.org"},{"name":"","address":"linux-arm-msm@vger.kernel.org"},{"name":"","address":"linux-kernel@vger.kernel.org"},{"name":"Kathiravan Thirumoorthy","address":"kathiravan.thirumoorthy@oss.qualcomm.com"},{"name":"","address":"stable@vger.kernel.org"}],"timestamp":{"raw":"2026-08-12T08:30:55.000Z","iso":"2026-08-12T08:30:55.000Z","valid":true},"subject":"[PATCH v2 1/2] i2c: qcom-geni: update frequency table to fix timing parameters","mailingLists":[{"id":"linux-i2c.vger.kernel.org","displayName":"linux-i2c.vger.kernel.org"}],"blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","text":"In IPQ5424, to meet the setup and hold timing requirements in the\nstandard mode, update the frequency table with the values recommended by\nHW design team."},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Also remove the stray space in the I2C_MAX_FAST_MODE_FREQ entry."},{"kind":"code","text":"Cc: <stable@vger.kernel.org>\nFixes: 85c34532849d (\"i2c: qcom-geni: fix I2C frequency table to achieve accurate bus rates\")\nFixes: 506bb2ab0075 (\"i2c: qcom-geni: Support systems with 32MHz serial engine clock\")"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Signed-off-by: Kathiravan Thirumoorthy <kathiravan.thirumoorthy@oss.qualcomm.com>"},{"kind":"patch","patchId":"patch:20260812-ipq5424_i2c_scl_updates-v2-1-e09cd39d01d7@oss.qualcomm.com:1:0"}],"patchIds":["patch:20260812-ipq5424_i2c_scl_updates-v2-1-e09cd39d01d7@oss.qualcomm.com:1:0"],"attachmentMetadata":[],"sourceOrdinal":1,"diagnostics":[],"declaredParentMessageId":"20260812-ipq5424_i2c_scl_updates-v2-0-e09cd39d01d7@oss.qualcomm.com","parentId":"20260812-ipq5424_i2c_scl_updates-v2-0-e09cd39d01d7@oss.qualcomm.com"},"20260812-ipq5424_i2c_scl_updates-v2-2-e09cd39d01d7@oss.qualcomm.com":{"id":"20260812-ipq5424_i2c_scl_updates-v2-2-e09cd39d01d7@oss.qualcomm.com","messageId":"20260812-ipq5424_i2c_scl_updates-v2-2-e09cd39d01d7@oss.qualcomm.com","references":["20260812-ipq5424_i2c_scl_updates-v2-0-e09cd39d01d7@oss.qualcomm.com"],"missingAncestorIds":[],"author":{"name":"Kathiravan Thirumoorthy","address":"kathiravan.thirumoorthy@oss.qualcomm.com"},"replyTo":[],"to":[{"name":"Mukesh Kumar Savaliya","address":"mukesh.savaliya@oss.qualcomm.com"},{"name":"Viken Dadhaniya","address":"viken.dadhaniya@oss.qualcomm.com"},{"name":"Andi Shyti","address":"andi.shyti@kernel.org"},{"name":"Manikanta Mylavarapu","address":"quic_mmanikan@quicinc.com"},{"name":"Bjorn Andersson","address":"andersson@kernel.org"},{"name":"Konrad Dybcio","address":"konradybcio@kernel.org"}],"cc":[{"name":"Mukesh Kumar Savaliya","address":"quic_msavaliy@quicinc.com"},{"name":"","address":"linux-i2c@vger.kernel.org"},{"name":"","address":"linux-arm-msm@vger.kernel.org"},{"name":"","address":"linux-kernel@vger.kernel.org"},{"name":"Kathiravan Thirumoorthy","address":"kathiravan.thirumoorthy@oss.qualcomm.com"}],"timestamp":{"raw":"2026-08-12T08:30:56.000Z","iso":"2026-08-12T08:30:56.000Z","valid":true},"subject":"[PATCH v2 2/2] i2c: qcom-geni: add I2C frequency table for 32 MHz firmware-based SEs","mailingLists":[{"id":"linux-i2c.vger.kernel.org","displayName":"linux-i2c.vger.kernel.org"}],"blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","text":"On IPQ5424, the I2C controller can operate on both RTL-hardened SEs\nand firmware-based SEs. As documented in commit 506bb2ab0075\n(\"i2c: qcom-geni: Support systems with 32MHz serial engine clock\"),\nin IPQ5424 SEs use a 32 MHz source clock."},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"The existing frequency table does not provide the required SCL timing\nparameters for firmware-based SEs. Add a dedicated frequency table\nusing the SCL counter values recommended by the hardware design team\nand select it for firmware-based SEs to achieve the target bus\nfrequencies."},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Move geni_i2c_clk_map_idx() from geni_i2c_resources_init() to\ngeni_i2c_init() to ensure SE_HW_PARAM_2 is accessed only after the\nrequired clocks have been enabled."},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Signed-off-by: Kathiravan Thirumoorthy <kathiravan.thirumoorthy@oss.qualcomm.com>"},{"kind":"patch","patchId":"patch:20260812-ipq5424_i2c_scl_updates-v2-2-e09cd39d01d7@oss.qualcomm.com:2:0"}],"patchIds":["patch:20260812-ipq5424_i2c_scl_updates-v2-2-e09cd39d01d7@oss.qualcomm.com:2:0"],"attachmentMetadata":[],"sourceOrdinal":2,"diagnostics":[],"declaredParentMessageId":"20260812-ipq5424_i2c_scl_updates-v2-0-e09cd39d01d7@oss.qualcomm.com","parentId":"20260812-ipq5424_i2c_scl_updates-v2-0-e09cd39d01d7@oss.qualcomm.com"},"eef12701-e916-4c4a-9dc2-2b6836e7cf59@oss.qualcomm.com":{"id":"eef12701-e916-4c4a-9dc2-2b6836e7cf59@oss.qualcomm.com","messageId":"eef12701-e916-4c4a-9dc2-2b6836e7cf59@oss.qualcomm.com","references":["20260812-ipq5424_i2c_scl_updates-v2-0-e09cd39d01d7@oss.qualcomm.com","20260812-ipq5424_i2c_scl_updates-v2-1-e09cd39d01d7@oss.qualcomm.com"],"missingAncestorIds":[],"author":{"name":"Mukesh Savaliya","address":"mukesh.savaliya@oss.qualcomm.com"},"replyTo":[],"to":[{"name":"Kathiravan Thirumoorthy","address":"kathiravan.thirumoorthy@oss.qualcomm.com"},{"name":"Viken Dadhaniya","address":"viken.dadhaniya@oss.qualcomm.com"},{"name":"Andi Shyti","address":"andi.shyti@kernel.org"},{"name":"Manikanta Mylavarapu","address":"quic_mmanikan@quicinc.com"},{"name":"Bjorn Andersson","address":"andersson@kernel.org"},{"name":"Konrad Dybcio","address":"konradybcio@kernel.org"}],"cc":[{"name":"Mukesh Kumar Savaliya","address":"quic_msavaliy@quicinc.com"},{"name":"","address":"linux-i2c@vger.kernel.org"},{"name":"","address":"linux-arm-msm@vger.kernel.org"},{"name":"","address":"linux-kernel@vger.kernel.org"},{"name":"","address":"stable@vger.kernel.org"}],"timestamp":{"raw":"2026-08-12T17:45:54.000Z","iso":"2026-08-12T17:45:54.000Z","valid":true},"subject":"Re: [PATCH v2 1/2] i2c: qcom-geni: update frequency table to fix timing parameters","mailingLists":[{"id":"linux-i2c.vger.kernel.org","displayName":"linux-i2c.vger.kernel.org"}],"blocks":[{"kind":"quote","attribution":"On 8/12/2026 2:00 PM, Kathiravan Thirumoorthy wrote:","lines":[{"depth":1,"tex